spoint singleplayer cold-boot (gh-pages BrowserServer Web Worker) is dominated by worker connect >10s = worker module-graph fetch + Jolt WASM cold start, ALL upstream of the LoadingMachine curtain gates - so the win pattern is 'overlap X with the worker boot', not gate-tuning. A startup-bottleneck-hunt workflow (.claude/workflows scripts) confirmed 16/27 bottlenecks. SHIPPED + witnessed: (1) ModelPoolAdapter.progressiveReady HEAD not GET (was downloading the whole baked root twice to probe existence; 405/501->GET fallback). (2) WorkerEntry Jolt physics.init() kicked as physicsReady promise overlapping app eval, awaited before tick; ALSO top-level getJolt() warm (exported from World.js) so WASM compile starts at worker module-load before INIT. (3) WorkerEntry app loads Promise.all not serial await. (4) BrowserServer dropped ?v=Date.now() worker cache-buster (defeated HTTP cache every load; host ETag/Last-Modified revalidates). (5) ModelPool workerCount:2 (was up-to-8 LOD workers each blob-importing draco-loader.js contending with env download). (6) app.js _finishLoading hides curtain BEFORE warmupShaders (now background; el.onMeshReady keeps incremental warmup). (7) World.js browser getJolt imports jolt-physics.wasm.js (1.2MB+streamed 1.87MB .wasm, compileStreaming) not the 3.7MB base64 wasm-compat; Node keeps wasm-compat; gh-pages already copies whole jolt dist so .wasm ships - VERIFY no 404/MIME on deployed. (8) BIGGEST WIN app.js: right after the world-module import (before client/worker construction) fire-and-forget GET each app==='environment' model's .prog/model.progressive.glb into HTTP cache (singleplayer too) - witnessed browser-24 prog warm at 833ms, snapshot-time ModelPool spawn fetches are cache HITS transfer:0. Do NOT un-gate prefetchModels (raw GLB, re-adds wasted parse). (9) player VRM initAssets kicked right after world import (during boot), _assetsKicked guard. (10) firstSnapshotEntityPending seeded only for environment/noAutoLod entities so props dont hold the curtain. ORANGE CUBE root cause (user-reported): NOT AppPhysics fallbackBox (invisible body) - it was EntityLoader.js:142 buildEntityMesh drawing a 0xff8800 box when entityState.model empty on the cold worker (env entity in first snapshot before model resolves) then marking loaded so the real model never replaced it; fix = skip+defer for non-deliberate-primitive app===environment entity with no model yet. Commits 7eca2ec5-area: 7bb4aa15(A) 292c452b(B) 5aebeb69(C) d5053a72(orange). Local warm-cache timeline can't show these wins (no network/WASM cost); they land on the deployed cold path - witness deployed.